# A Docker build needs the workspace manifest, the lockfile, the toolchain pin and the crate
# sources. `target/` alone would make every build hand gigabytes to the daemon before it starts,
# and compose builds this image with the repository root as its context (see
# docs/examples/gateway-oidc/compose.yaml), so the exclusions belong here rather than beside the
# Dockerfile.

target/
.git/
.github/
.superpowers/
docs/
dev/

# The front end is installed and built inside the image (the Dockerfile's web-build stage): a host's
# node_modules carries host-platform binaries its `npm run build` cannot run, and a host's web/dist
# would bake in a page the build inside did not make.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
